    "invariants": [
      "Exactly one authoritative owner may mutate a task at a time.",
      "Every mutation uses revision and CAS semantics.",
      "Every effectful execution binds an idempotency key.",
      "Stale leases and stale fencing tokens cannot complete.",
      "A provider-unknown outcome enters reconciliation rather than blind retry.",
      "A task can terminalize only once.",
      "A merge requires current validation evidence.",
      "A rescue or retry cannot erase an observed external effect.",
      "Owner restart reconstructs the same authoritative state from durable data.",
      "A controller cannot bypass the state-transition service by directly updating task tables.",
      "Transition events and current materialized state must reconcile.",
      "No successful terminal state may exist without its required receipt.",
      "A failed validation cannot become success through merge bookkeeping.",
      "A policy change does not retroactively authorize an earlier invocation."
    ],
